# Install

Install the toolchain on this machine, clone the repository, and verify
with one preview. There is no crates.io package and no install script.

:note[title: "Checkout commands"] {{
    Until an installed `rocci` exists, the canonical spelling is
    `cargo run -p rocci-cli --` from the repository root. Later pages
    write `rocci view` and `rocci run`; prefix those the same way.
}}

This manual does not teach programming from zero. You should be able to
read typed code, use a terminal and Git, and edit a text file.

## Toolchain

| Tool | Role | As tested |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Rust and Cargo | Build the Rocci workspace | GitHub Actions `dtolnay/rust-toolchain@stable`, edition 2024 crates |
| Roc nightly | Compile generated and authored Roc | `nightly-2026-08-26` (`b29bef3`), pinned in `docker/install-roc.sh` |
| Datastar JS | Browser transport copied by `run` | `1.0.2` in application `rocci.toml` |
| Native webview | Preview window | macOS WebKit, Linux WebKitGTK 4.1, Windows system webview |

The [support matrix](/docs/reference/compatibility/) also lists editors,
packaging, and known limits. A mismatched Roc nightly can reject syntax
that is valid for this repository.

Optional primers: [Roc](/docs/appendix/roc-for-rocci/),
[Datastar](/docs/appendix/web-foundations/). Full Roc lives at
[roc-lang.org](https://www.roc-lang.org/).

## Install Rust and Roc

Install a Rust toolchain that compiles this workspace (edition 2024).
[rustup](https://rustup.rs/) is the usual path.

Install Roc. This repository is tested against **Roc nightly-2026-08-26**
(`b29bef3`). See the [Roc install docs](https://www.roc-lang.org/install)
and match that nightly when a listed nightly is available. Confirm:

```sh
roc version
rustc --version
```

## Clone and build

```sh
git clone https://github.com/koliyo/rocci.git
cd rocci
cargo build -p rocci-cli
```

## Desktop preview

:tabs.begin[group: "install-os", kind: "platform"]
    :tab[id: "mac", label: "macOS"] {{
        Tao and Wry use the system WebKit view. No extra webview packages.
        Ad-hoc `.app` bundling is available later with `rocci bundle`.
        Verified in CI (`macos-latest`).
    }}
    :tab[id: "linux", label: "Linux"] {{
        Install the WebKitGTK development packages Wry needs. On Debian and
        Ubuntu this matches CI (`ubuntu-latest`):

        ```sh
        sudo apt-get update
        sudo apt-get install -y \
          libgtk-3-dev libwebkit2gtk-4.1-dev \
          libappindicator3-dev librsvg2-dev patchelf
        ```

        Other distributions use their WebKitGTK 4.1 development packages.
        Headless checks can pass `--no-window`.
    }}
    :tab[id: "windows", label: "Windows"] {{
        Wry uses the operating-system webview. Windows packaging is not
        implemented. Development `rocci run` / `rocci view` use the same local
        HTTP server as other platforms. This path is not in CI.
    }}
:tabs.end

## Verify

From the repository root:

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- --help
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- view \
  examples/rocci/standalone/styling/Styling.rocci \
  --component Hello --no-window
```

The view command prints a local URL (default port `8000` with
`--no-window`). Open it, or drop `--no-window` to use the native window.
You should see a greeting. If `roc` is missing or the webview fails to
link, see [install failures](/docs/troubleshooting/install/).

### Experimental GitHub archives

CI publishes `rocci-{version}-{target}.tar.gz` archives on GitHub Releases
(macOS aarch64 and Linux x86_64). Treat them as **experimental**. They are
not the first-run path in this manual.

Next: [Rocci in five minutes](/docs/five-minutes/).
